# Generated by the slddRoundTrip test — edited .sldd emitted for MATLAB verification
test/fixtures/rt_out/

# The integration suite makes its working copies BESIDE the four source fixtures in
# this directory (`fs.copy(wsUri('data.sldd'), wsUri('json_undo_paint_copy.sldd'))`)
# and deletes them in teardown, so a green run leaves nothing behind. A test that
# throws before its teardown does, and because the directory is otherwise tracked,
# that leftover is untracked-and-not-ignored — exactly what a blind `git add -A`
# sweeps into a commit.
#
# Ignoring the directory and re-admitting the sources, rather than listing the
# artifacts: there are already seventeen working-copy names across ten suite files,
# one of them containing a space, and each new test invents another. A deny-list
# needs updating by whoever adds the next one, which is the person who will not know
# it exists. A new SOURCE fixture now needs `git add -f` once — a discoverable
# prompt, unlike silently committed detritus.
#
# Ignore rules do not apply to already-tracked files, so this hides nothing: the
# suite rewrites data.sldd in place, and a run that corrupted it would still show up
# as a normal modification.
test-integration/fixtures/workspace/*
!test-integration/fixtures/workspace/binary.sldd
!test-integration/fixtures/workspace/data.sldd
!test-integration/fixtures/workspace/model.slx
!test-integration/fixtures/workspace/params.sldd

